create a REST API service for the admin panel of a chat application using ejabberd as the XMPP server and postgreSQL to store the admin settings, the admin panel allows the user to register Operators, create Groups and add the Operators to one or more Groups, the groups represent ejabberd's Multi-User Chat (MUC) and the operators represent Clients/Users registered on the ejabberd server. That means, everytime you add a new operator in the admin panel an user is created on the XMPP server and everytime a group is created in the admin panel a mult-user chat room is created on the server. Create endpoints to make this possible.

There is a operators table in the PostgreSQL database, when you add a new Operator in the admin panel not only a user should be created on the XMPP server but it should insert a new Operator into the operators table in the database, the operators table has two field id (uuid primary key, should be autogenerated) and name (varchar a display name of the Operator)

There is a groups table in the PostgreSQL database, when you create a new Group in the admin panel not only a multi-user chat room should be created on the XMPP server but it should insert a new Group into the groups table in the database, the groups table has two field id (uuid primary key, should be autogenerated) and name (varchar a display name of the Group)

There is a operator_groups table in the PostgreSQL database, when you add a operator to a group in the admin panel not only the user representing the operator should be added to the multi-user chat room on the XMPP server but a new row should be inserted into the operator_groups table with the id of the operator and the id of the group as foreign keys for the operators and groups table